# Why did Rome fall?
subtitle: "Why the Western Roman Empire collapsed while the East lasted another thousand years: no single cause, just money, then soldiers, then control."
thumb: "band \"Not the lead pipes\" stamp \"210 SUSPECTS\" card cork"

## Why did Rome fall?
sources:
    - id: demandt
      title: 'Der Fall Roms: Die Auflösung des römischen Reiches im Urteil der Nachwelt'
      authors: Alexander Demandt
      year: 1984
      finding: Catalogues 210 explanations that have been offered for Rome's fall.
    - id: heather
      title: 'The Fall of the Roman Empire: A New History of Rome and the Barbarians'
      authors: Peter Heather
      year: 2005
      finding: The loss of Africa (439) and other rich provinces cut the West's tax revenue and with it its armies.
    - id: wardperkins
      title: The Fall of Rome and the End of Civilization
      authors: Bryan Ward-Perkins
      year: 2005
      finding: 'Archaeology shows a steep fall in western living standards: cruder pottery, fewer coins, smaller cattle.'
    - id: crisis
      title: Crisis of the Third Century
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2026
      finding: '235–284: over 50 claimants to the throne, about half recognised; almost all legitimate emperors died violently.'
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century
    - id: britannica
      title: Fall of Rome
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2024
      finding: '476: Odoacer deposes Romulus Augustulus; the Eastern empire lasts until 1453.'

